# Program Logic Rule
# This rule explains the data flow and feature engineering logic of the UFC fight prediction program

LANGUAGE: Python
DATABASE: PostgreSQL
MAIN_FILE: main.py

# Data Flow Overview
The program follows a sequential data processing pipeline:

1. DATA INGESTION:
   - Read competitions.csv and individuals.csv (fighters data)
   - Load data into PostgreSQL database in the features schema
   - Create core mapping tables: fighter_mapping, fight_mapping, event_mapping
   - Create fight_stats_core table with one row per fighter per fight

2. FEATURE ENGINEERING LAYER 1:
   - Create fight_stats_fe table by copying fight_stats_core
   - Add basic engineered features:
     - time_sec: Fight duration in seconds
     - ko: Knockout indicator
     - sub_land: Submission success indicator
     - win: Win/loss indicator
     - age: Fighter age at time of fight
     - days_since_last_fight: Time since previous fight
     - reach: Fighter reach
     - height: Fighter height
     - ape: Ape index (reach/height ratio)
     - ufcage: Fighter experience in UFC

3. FEATURE ENGINEERING LAYER 2:
   - Create fight_stats_derived table
   - Consolidate round-by-round stats into fight totals
   - Preserve round 1 stats separately (e.g., sig_str_land_rd1)
   - Add derived metrics:
     - _acc: Accuracy ratios (landed/attempted)
     - _def: Defense ratios
     - _per_min: Rate statistics
     - _ratio: Fighter performance relative to opponent

4. FEATURE-SPECIFIC TABLES:
   - Break out each stat into dedicated tables (e.g., features.td, features.sig_str)
   - Each table contains all derived metrics for that stat
   - Create separate tables for round 1 stats (e.g., features.td_rd1)
   - Add advanced derived features:
     - _avg: Career averages
     - _sdev: Standard deviations
     - _dec_avg: Time-decay weighted averages (1.5yr half-life)
     - _opp_avg: Opponent performance averages
     - _adjperf: Adjusted performance metrics

# Table Progression
PROGRESSION:
  1. features.fight_stats_core: Raw fight statistics from CSV
  2. features.fight_stats_fe: First layer of engineered features
  3. features.fight_stats_derived: Consolidated fight totals and basic derived metrics
  4. features.<stat> and features.<stat>_rd1: Feature-specific tables with all derived metrics

# Calculator Sequence
CALCULATORS:
  - Base calculators: TimeSecCalculator, KOCalculator, SubmissionslandCalculator, WinCalculator, etc.
  - Derived calculators: AccuracyCalculator, DefenseCalculator, PerMinCalculator, RatioCalculator
  - Advanced calculators: AverageCalculator, StandardDeviationCalculator, TimedecAvgCalculator, AdjustedPerformanceCalculator

# Training Data Creation
FINAL_STEPS:
  - CreateTrainingData: Assembles features from all tables into training dataset
  - CleanTrainingData: Handles missing values and prepares final dataset
  - Output: data/training_data.csv for model training